Interview Tips for These Questions

When answering, keep these principles in mind:

Always explain the business problem first. Interviewers want to know why the service exists, not just the technology.

State your ownership clearly. Use "I designed...", "I implemented...", "I optimized...", and distinguish your work from the team's.

Discuss trade-offs. Mention why you chose one approach over alternatives (e.g., Kafka vs. REST, choreography vs. orchestration).

Include production experience. Talk about monitoring, failures, retries, scaling, and lessons learned.

Be honest about scope. If you collaborated on an area rather than owning it end-to-end, say so.


These answers are consistent with your experience and should stand up well to follow-up questions in a senior Java/Spring Boot interview.
